    "sidechain-ducker": {
      "name": "Sidechain Ducker",
      "description": "Turns `in` down while another signal, the `sidechain`, is loud: music that dips under a voice-over, or a pad that pumps with the kick drum. Both inputs take mono or stereo.\n\n- `in` (audio): the signal that gets turned down.\n- `sidechain` (audio): the signal that does the turning down. It is only listened to, never heard; mix it in separately if you want to hear it.\n- `threshold` (dB): how loud the sidechain must get to duck `in`. The ducking lets go once the sidechain falls 6 dB below it.\n- `amount` (dB): how far `in` drops while the sidechain is loud.\n- `attack` (seconds): how quickly `in` dips when the sidechain gets loud (about 63 % of the dip in this time).\n- `release` (seconds): how quickly `in` comes back afterwards, measured the same way; longer releases make a slower swell, short ones a tight pump.\n\nInside: an Envelope Follower (instant attack, 10 ms release) measures the sidechain's peak level in decibels, and a Compare with 6 dB of hysteresis decides whether it counts as loud. A Switch picks 0 dB or minus `amount`, and a Smooth glides between them, falling with the attack time and rising with the release time, into the Gain on `in`.",
      "version": 1,
      "author": "Audio Constructor",
      "tags": [
        "dynamics",
        "sidechain",
        "ducking",
        "mixing"
      ],
      "source": "shipped:sidechain-ducker",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "in",
          "type": "audio",
          "targets": [
            "6:in"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "sidechain",
          "type": "audio",
          "targets": [
            "1:in"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "threshold",
          "type": "float",
          "unit": "db",
          "default": -30.0,
          "range": [
            -60.0,
            0.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "2:b"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "amount",
          "type": "float",
          "unit": "db",
          "default": 12.0,
          "range": [
            0.0,
            48.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "3:in"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "attack",
          "type": "float",
          "unit": "seconds",
          "default": 0.01,
          "range": [
            0.0,
            0.5
          ],
          "targets": [
            "5:fall"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "release",
          "type": "float",
          "unit": "seconds",
          "default": 0.3,
          "range": [
            0.0,
            2.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "5:rise"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "out",
          "type": "audio",
          "source": "6:out"
        }
      ],
      "graph": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "id": "1",
            "kind": "envelope_follower",
            "params": {
              "attack": 0.0,
              "mode": "peak",
              "release": 0.01
            },
            "ui": {
              "pos": [
                0.0,
                0.0
              ],
              "label": "Sidechain level"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "2",
            "kind": "compare",
            "params": {
              "hysteresis": 6.0,
              "op": "greater"
            },
            "ui": {
              "pos": [
                220.0,
                0.0
              ],
              "label": "Loud?"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "3",
            "kind": "unary",
            "params": {
              "op": "negate"
            },
            "ui": {
              "pos": [
                220.0,
                160.0
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "4",
            "kind": "switch",
            "config": {
              "type": "float"
            },
            "params": {
              "a": 0.0
            },
            "ui": {
              "pos": [
                440.0,
                0.0
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "5",
            "kind": "smooth",
            "params": {
              "mode": "exponential"
            },
            "ui": {
              "pos": [
                660.0,
                0.0
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "6",
            "kind": "gain",
            "ui": {
              "pos": [
                880.0,
                160.0
              ]
            }
          }
        ],
        "wires": [
          {
            "from": "1:level_db",
            "to": "2:a"
          },
          {
            "from": "2:out",
            "to": "4:select"
          },
          {
            "from": "3:out",
            "to": "4:b"
          },
          {
            "from": "4:out",
            "to": "5:in"
          },
          {
            "from": "5:out",
            "to": "6:gain"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "subtractive-synth-voice": {
      "name": "Subtractive Synth Voice",
      "description": "One voice of a classic subtractive synth: two detuned sawtooth oscillators, a resonant ladder filter swept by an envelope, and the same envelope on the volume. It is a body for a Voices node: tick **Polyphonic** on its Node tab to make it one and wire MIDI into its `midi` input for a polyphonic synth that plays chords, pads, leads, and basses.\n\n- `cutoff` (Hz) is where the filter sits while the envelope is at rest; `resonance` (0 to 1) adds a peak there, and near 1 the filter starts to whistle.\n- `env_amount` (octaves) is how far the envelope opens the filter above `cutoff` at its peak: 3 means three octaves (eight times the frequency). Negative values close the filter instead.\n- `attack`, `decay`, and `release` (seconds) and `sustain` (0 to 1) shape the envelope. It sweeps the filter and sets the volume at once, so a short decay with a low sustain makes a pluck, and a slow attack makes a pad.\n- `detune` (cents) pulls the two oscillators apart, one up and one down by half of it, for a thicker, beating sound; 0 makes them one.\n- `level` (dB) is the voice's loudness, and each note's velocity scales it. The voices of a Voices node add up, so turn it down for big chords.\n- `out` is the voice, mono.\n\nInside: a Voice node gives the note's frequency, gate, and velocity. Half of `detune`, in semitones, becomes a frequency ratio (Convert) that divides one Oscillator's frequency and multiplies the other's. A Mix adds the two saws at −9 dB each, and a 24 dB per octave Ladder filters them. An ADSR follows the gate: multiplied by `env_amount` it is an offset in octaves, 2 raised to it multiplies `cutoff`, and the envelope times velocity drives the VCA, a Math multiply on the filtered sound, followed by a Gain for `level`.",
      "version": 1,
      "author": "Audio Constructor",
      "tags": [
        "synth",
        "instrument",
        "subtractive",
        "polyphonic",
        "filter"
      ],
      "source": "shipped:subtractive-synth-voice",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "cutoff",
          "type": "float",
          "unit": "hz",
          "default": 500.0,
          "range": [
            20.0,
            20000.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "f:a"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "resonance",
          "type": "float",
          "default": 0.3,
          "range": [
            0.0,
            1.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "9:resonance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "env_amount",
          "type": "float",
          "default": 3.0,
          "range": [
            -4.0,
            8.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "d:b"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "attack",
          "type": "float",
          "unit": "seconds",
          "default": 0.005,
          "range": [
            0.0,
            10.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "c:attack"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "decay",
          "type": "float",
          "unit": "seconds",
          "default": 0.4,
          "range": [
            0.0,
            10.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "c:decay"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "sustain",
          "type": "float",
          "default": 0.5,
          "range": [
            0.0,
            1.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "c:sustain"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "release",
          "type": "float",
          "unit": "seconds",
          "default": 0.3,
          "range": [
            0.0,
            20.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "c:release"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "detune",
          "type": "float",
          "default": 12.0,
          "range": [
            0.0,
            100.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "2:a"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "level",
          "type": "float",
          "unit": "db",
          "default": 0.0,
          "range": [
            -60.0,
            12.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "b:gain"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "out",
          "type": "audio",
          "source": "b:out"
        }
      ],
      "graph": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "id": "1",
